 "result_text": "`scval.to_struct` now sorts its keys, which should fix the failing `add_prices` call. I haven't run anything, including your reproduction against testnet, so it's untested.\n\nThe XDR in your report has the struct's fields in the order `source, asset, price, timestamp`. As far as I know, Soroban requires map keys to be sorted, and the Rust SDK sorts struct fields alphabetically. Unsorted keys would explain the `failed to convert ScVal to host value` error, though I haven't confirmed that against the host.\n\nThe change is in `stellar_sdk/scval.py`, in `to_struct`: it now builds the map from `sorted(data.items(), ...)`.\n\n`to_map` is unchanged, so a map built directly with `to_map` still keeps whatever order you give it. Sorting there would mean comparing arbitrary `SCVal` keys, so I left it alone.",
